WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.740
This walkthrough compares the previous
certification basis workflow with the

2
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.850
updated application.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.570
In the previous TPMS, related tasks were
spread across four maintenance areas.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.830
Master Cert Basis held
the code and description.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.020
Cert Basis attached
regulations to that Master,

6
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.190
using Add or Bulk Add.

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.550
Spreadsheet Import provided
another way to add regulations,

8
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:30.420
while Master Cert Basis Associate
linked the Basis to TCCA projects.

9
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.000
Maintaining the record meant moving between
these areas and opening the relevant

10
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.030
Update screens.

11
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.060
The Cert Basis listing also displayed
one row for each regulation link,

12
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.450
repeating the same Master
code and description.

13
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.250
In the updated application, the
area is called Certification Basis.

14
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.450
Each Basis appears once in the
listing, alongside its description,

15
00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.100
regulation count and project usage count.

16
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.790
Search helps us find the record, and
clicking its code opens the details.

17
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.830
To create a Basis, select Add.

18
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.090
Creation follows two steps.

19
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.970
First, enter the Basis
code and description,

20
00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.710
the same identity previously
created in Master Cert Basis.

21
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.850
This step adds dedicated optional
reference fields for the TCDS number,

22
00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.130
source link and Basis statement
as written in the document.

23
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.340
An optional source PDF upload is
available alongside these references.

24
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.690
Select Continue to choose the regulations.

25
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.010
The searchable list identifies
each existing rule by its section,

26
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.630
amendment and title.

27
00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:38.800
Select one rule, or tick several,
then use Add selected to include them

28
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.590
together. The selected regulations
appear in the table below.

29
00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.810
Review the list, remove
any unwanted entries,

30
00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.830
and check the Basis details
before selecting Create Basis.

31
00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:54.310
After creation, return to the
listing and reopen the same Basis.

32
00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:59.470
Regulations shows the selected rules,
and opening a rule displays its saved

33
00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.060
requirement text in a readable side panel.

34
00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:06.790
To adjust the selection later, choose
Edit and use the same control to add

35
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.940
further regulations.

36
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:13.710
For an existing shared Basis, Used By
shows the TCCA projects that use it,

37
00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.260
with links to the relevant GCP workflow.

38
00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:20.580
Project association remains
managed within GCP Projects.

39
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.990
The spreadsheet Import option is also
retained for adding a prepared regulation

40
00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.920
list to an existing Basis.

41
00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:29.840
The result is a clearer
route through the work:

42
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:34.600
find the Basis, review its references,
select the appropriate regulations,

43
00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.200
and see where the shared record is used.
